From 5f8bbddc6c856fc501e23268f78d5fa566d5ff18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:07:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] d/steamvr_lh, ipc: backport live device hotplug for WiVRn

Based on Eidenz's Monado hotplug implementation through 47551c4b2 and the
threading/chirality adaptations in 1ee366b8c from the local monado-1 fork.
Keep the pinned upstream API and WiVRn recording/prediction patches.

Publish devices only after WiVRn installs its space callback, retain a
context even when startup finds no devices, and stop publication before
session teardown. Refresh per-client device proxies before resolving new
role indices. Callback hand trackers re-resolve their sources at locate.
Keep upstream invalid-pose handling rather than importing the fork's
hold-pose policy or its screenshot/UDCAP features.
